# Second follow-up to -16/-17. -16 (good, chained play/wait/state) died at ~9s
# and looked stuck dead for the next ~33s across three near-bare state reads.
# -17 (no play at all) never died, so it could not test revival. This gets the
# player killed with one short play call, then polls with nothing but bare
# wait/state after -- no play() at all past that point -- to separate a real
# stall from another unlucky sampling run of a fast re-death loop.
open
tap battleground
tap map:conquest
tap class:druid:balance
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state

play good 15
shot died
state

wait 5
state
shot p1

wait 5
state
shot p2

wait 5
state
shot p3

wait 5
state
shot p4

wait 5
state
shot p5

wait 5
state
shot p6
